    "faq": {
      "title": "Frequently asked questions",
      "items": [
        {
          "question": "How does Nautik work?",
          "answer": "Nautik is a platform that lets you search and book moorings at the best ports. Just select a port, dates and, if you are registered, your vessel. We will show you availability and prices so you can book safely."
        },
        {
          "question": "When do I need to check in?",
          "answer": "Check-in takes place on the day of arrival at the port, usually from 12:00. We recommend contacting the port in advance to confirm the exact time."
        },
        {
          "question": "Can I deduct VAT from the booking?",
          "answer": "It depends on your tax situation. If you are self-employed or a company and the boat is used for economic activity, you can consult your advisor. We issue invoices with VAT broken down."
        },
        {
          "question": "What happens if I don't bring the documentation?",
          "answer": "It is mandatory to present the boat's documentation (navigation permit, insurance, etc.) at check-in. If you don't bring it, the port may deny you access to the mooring."
        },
        {
          "question": "Do I need a passport if I come from another country?",
          "answer": "If you come from a country outside the Schengen area, you may need a passport. For EU citizens, only a valid national ID or identity document is required."
        },
        {
          "question": "How do I become a regular customer?",
          "answer": "Register on our website and complete your profile. By making recurring bookings, you will accumulate points and gain access to exclusive discounts for regular customers."
        },
        {
          "question": "Can I use the services without being a customer?",
          "answer": "Yes, you can search ports and check availability without registering. But to book you will need to create an account and, if you have a vessel, register it."
        },
        {
          "question": "Are there moorings for seaplanes?",
          "answer": "Currently our partner ports do not have specific moorings for seaplanes. All our moorings are for conventional vessels."
        }
      ]
    }
  },
